3) User-space program (C) — read device and publish to MQTT

You can use libmosquitto for MQTT or simply call system("mosquitto_pub ..."). Using libmosquitto is cleaner.

Example ultrasonic_user.c using libmosquitto:

// ultrasonic_user.c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <mosquitto.h>

#define DEV_PATH "/dev/ultrasonic0"
#define BUF_LEN 64

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    int fd = open(DEV_PATH, O_RDONLY);
    if (fd < 0) {
        perror("open");
        return 1;
    }

    struct mosquitto *mosq;
    mosquitto_lib_init();
    mosq = mosquitto_new(NULL, true, NULL);
    if (!mosq) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to create mosquitto instance\n");
        close(fd);
        return 1;
    }
    // Connect to local broker
    if (mosquitto_connect(mosq, "localhost", 1883, 60)) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Could not connect to broker\n");
        mosquitto_destroy(mosq);
        close(fd);
        return 1;
    }

    char buf[BUF_LEN];
    while (1) {
        lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_SET);
        ssize_t n = read(fd, buf, BUF_LEN-1);
        if (n > 0) {
            buf[n] = 0;
            // optional parse: "DIST:xx.xx\n"
            printf("Read: %s", buf);
            // Publish to topic
            mosquitto_publish(mosq, NULL, "parking/slot1/distance", strlen(buf), buf, 0, false);
        } else {
            // no data, wait
            sleep(1);
        }
        mosquitto_loop(mosq, 0, 1);
        sleep(1);
    }

    mosquitto_destroy(mosq);
    mosquitto_lib_cleanup();
    close(fd);
    return 0;
}


Build:

gcc -o ultrasonic_user ultrasonic_user.c -lmosquitto


Run:

sudo ./ultrasonic_user


You can then use mosquitto_sub -t 'parking/#' -v to see messages, or connect Node-RED / MQTT Explorer.

4) How to test (step-by-step)

Setup hardware: connect HC-SR04 Trig to GPIO (configured trig), Echo to echo GPIO (use level shifting if needed). Power sensor from 5V but ensure GPIO inputs tolerant — better use voltage divider on Echo (HC-SR04 echo is 5V on many boards). Safety first.

Build module: make → sudo insmod ultrasonic_drv.ko

Check dmesg for messages (module loaded, major number, etc.).

Confirm character device exists: /dev/ultrasonic0 (if not, create device node with mknod using the major printed by dmesg).

Run user-space daemon: sudo ./ultrasonic_user. It will open /dev/ultrasonic0 and publish readings to MQTT.

Observe logs: use mosquitto_sub -h localhost -t 'parking/#' -v or MQTT Explorer.

Manual read: sudo cat /dev/ultrasonic0 should display something like DIST:23.45.

Tweak sample rate: write to device echo "PERIOD 200" > /dev/ultrasonic0 to set sampling to 200ms.

